    {
      "id": 35,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        2400,
        560
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        560
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 39,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Pixel sprite + driving video -> sprite sheet (SCAIL 2)\n\nThe SCAIL 2 version of pixel-art/sprite-from-video: same inputs and outputs, a different motion model.\n1. Pixel sprite (blue): native pixel art (transparent or plain background); output keeps its pixel size + palette.\n2. Driving video (blue): one person doing the motion, whole body visible, static camera. Read at 16 fps, up to\n   81 frames (\"frame_load_cap\"; \"skip_first_frames\" to start later). Rounded down to 4n+1.\n3. Masks: SAM3 finds the person in the video (\"Driving video mask prompt\", default \"human\"); the sprite's own\n   silhouette is the reference mask, so creatures and robots work too. Check both in the mask previews.\n4. SCAIL 2 (animation mode) moves your character like the video. DPO LoRA + lightx2v distill LoRA, 6 steps,\n   CFG 1. Keep the prompt to one plain sentence; the video and the sprite do the work.\n5. Re-pixelate: \"height_match\" scales the clip once so the character in the FIRST frame has the sprite's height\n   (start the video in a neutral standing pose). Colours as in sprite-from-video.\n6. Sprite sheet: frame_step 2 keeps every 2nd frame; set max_frames / loop_trim for cycles.\nSaved to output/pixel/: sprite_from_video_scail2_*.png (sheet), .json (Aseprite), .webp, _preview.png,\nand the raw video (pixel/sprite_from_video_scail2_raw) to check the motion."
      ],
      "title": "READ ME"
    },
